From cbbe42c839ffd85c1e29132017e2e1ceb16584a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:22:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-302: gather pipelines walk slots fastest (slot-major
 workgroup order) so shared experts hit L2

Cell A (cellA-10051527): the multi-column gather is byte-identical but ALU-bound at real routing (padded
columns cost full loads+FMA), and the token-major order re-read a shared expert from DRAM at full cost
(pattern all g0 = pattern none g0). This keeps the NUM_COLS math and only permutes the (row block, slot)
workgroup set: consecutive linear workgroup ids walk the slots of one row block. Non-gather pipelines get
the same first_row expression through the WG_ROWBLOCK macro (identical source text).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 088636633d32c06feffc323c62b166d82ae71eab)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-302); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED on its own - supporting commit; see release ledger Table 1 W17, the number sits on that win's main commit
